1
00:01:48,979 --> 00:01:49,980
Day 1

2
00:01:57,080 --> 00:02:00,961
Day 2, Day 3, Day 4, Day 5

3
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:06,080
Shut up! I do have a grandpa!

4
00:02:06,549 --> 00:02:08,660
As if an old man could give birth to a wooden puppet!

5
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:10,220
Yeah, that's right!

6
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:12,540
I'm Grandpa's boy!

7
00:02:12,580 --> 00:02:13,980
Yay! My puppet!

8
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:16,560
Why, you...!

9
00:02:16,660 --> 00:02:18,320
What?

10
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:29,540
Help! Help me!

11
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:33,500
Goal!

12
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:36,820
Help! Don't score!

13
00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:45,460
(Children's sorrowful laughter)

14
00:02:45,710 --> 00:02:47,080
Heh, but look!

15
00:02:50,540 --> 00:02:58,140
Mokku, why don't you help him, huh? Mokku— Shut up! It's his fault! What do I care?!

16
00:02:58,780 --> 00:03:01,320
Mokku, you'll never become human acting like that!

17
00:03:01,945 --> 00:03:02,945
Human?

18
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:06,200
That's right. What will happen if you don't save him?

19
00:03:06,550 --> 00:03:09,200
There's no one else who can swim!

20
00:03:24,690 --> 00:03:25,690
Ah, Box!

21
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:35,140
Box!

22
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:36,240
What's wrong?!

23
00:03:36,944 --> 00:03:38,840
Hurry! Hurry! Hurry!

24
00:03:38,841 --> 00:03:39,841
Hurry!

25
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:25,760
Does Cathy really love me?

26
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:30,921
I don't care even if you're like a mother. No, I love you. I love you.

27
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:35,120
And I will stay by your side.

28
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:46,780
[[NO AUDIO]]

29
00:05:00,610 --> 00:05:04,080
It wasn't me. He's the one to blame for doing that first.

30
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:08,080
It's not my fault! He's the one who fell in.

31
00:05:19,290 --> 00:05:22,880
Cheer up. Don't be so down.

32
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:37,360
So it's really not my fault?

33
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:42,080
But...

34
00:05:44,650 --> 00:05:46,840
That's right, Mokku. Come on, Mokku.

35
00:05:47,255 --> 00:05:48,860
There's no need to brood over it.

36
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:52,760
That boy Cole fell into the river because the bridge was broken.

37
00:05:53,165 --> 00:05:57,480
You bravely jumped into the river to save him when no one else could.

38
00:05:57,780 --> 00:06:00,880
Of course I did. Huh? It doesn't bother me at all.

39
00:06:01,030 --> 00:06:04,360
Then let's hurry home. Grandpa is worried about you.

40
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:11,480
Why are you still moping around? It wasn't your fault. Brooding won't change anything.

41
00:06:11,820 --> 00:06:12,820
Shut up!

42
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:20,800
Stop putting on a tough act. You play pranks, but deep down, Mokku is a kind-hearted boy.

43
00:06:21,030 --> 00:06:22,960
Stop it! Get lost, all of you!

44
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:43,400
[[NO AUDIO]]

45
00:06:45,100 --> 00:06:47,720
Hey, Mokku, what are you trying to do?

46
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:54,100
I'm going to take Cole's place. —Huh? What did you say?

47
00:06:55,530 --> 00:06:56,940
If I become Cole,

48
00:06:57,085 --> 00:06:59,180
even Cole's mother will be happy.

49
00:06:59,940 --> 00:07:04,680
Don't be foolish. It's not that easy to become someone else's child.

50
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:12,300
Shut up! That way I'll have a mama, too, and maybe I could even become human!

51
00:07:13,165 --> 00:07:17,540
Good grief. Why do you always think only of yourself?

52
00:07:18,210 --> 00:07:21,660
Be quiet! You nag and complain way too much anyway!

53
00:07:23,660 --> 00:07:24,660
Right?!

54
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:32,300
What an idiot. He's only going to cause Cole's mother more grief.

55
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,000
Welcome home.

56
00:07:57,240 --> 00:07:58,640
(Sad music)

57
00:07:58,641 --> 00:07:59,641
Cole...

58
00:08:01,710 --> 00:08:04,500
(Sad music)

59
00:08:41,620 --> 00:08:42,620
Cole?

60
00:08:44,909 --> 00:08:49,520
I'm such a fool... As if Cole would ever come home.

61
00:08:52,940 --> 00:08:53,940
Who's there?

62
00:08:59,989 --> 00:09:02,080
Oh... Who are you?

63
00:09:03,740 --> 00:09:04,740
I came to see you.

64
00:09:05,039 --> 00:09:06,900
I was swept down the river with Cole.

65
00:09:08,910 --> 00:09:14,540
I, um... thought I could take Cole's place and comfort you, ma'am... Here.

66
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:18,520
Get out! I don't ever want to see your face!

67
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:19,920
Ma'am!

68
00:09:20,820 --> 00:09:21,820
Get out!

69
00:09:22,935 --> 00:09:24,120
I know the truth!

70
00:09:24,625 --> 00:09:28,680
If you hadn't thrown that stone, Cole wouldn't have slipped and fallen into the river!

71
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:32,100
Get out of here right now!

72
00:09:32,729 --> 00:09:34,620
And I'm going to kill her.

73
00:09:35,069 --> 00:09:37,200
She died in my place.

74
00:09:37,670 --> 00:09:38,670
She's a puppet girl.

75
00:10:04,719 --> 00:10:07,461
Oh, it started raining. How nice.

76
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:38,100
Please rest a little longer.

77
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:44,480
I'll be back.

78
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:12,100
Auntie!

79
00:11:18,199 --> 00:11:22,760
Where did he go in this rain?

80
00:11:28,855 --> 00:11:30,160
Again...

81
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:32,480
Where did he go in this rain?

82
00:11:46,759 --> 00:11:53,580
Looks like he came back. An old woman like me being so foolish... I feel terrible about what I did to him.

83
00:12:03,989 --> 00:12:09,900
In a place like this...

84
00:12:11,249 --> 00:12:13,100
What a silly boy...

85
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:38,320
Huh?

86
00:12:39,039 --> 00:12:42,080
Are you awake? Here, your lunch is ready.

87
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:44,340
Huh?

88
00:12:45,839 --> 00:12:47,900
Wash your face and put this on.

89
00:12:48,420 --> 00:12:50,560
I think it will fit you perfectly.

90
00:12:52,839 --> 00:12:56,040
What's the matter? Hurry up or you'll be late for school.

91
00:12:57,289 --> 00:13:00,100
A-Auntie, are you forgiving me?

92
00:13:04,780 --> 00:13:09,920
Thank you, Auntie! I'll be a good boy, I promise! I really promise!

93
00:13:21,319 --> 00:13:22,440
Whoa, incredible!

94
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:25,020
This is awesome!

95
00:13:25,520 --> 00:13:29,560
Hey, Mokku! You can't even taste anything anyway, can you? Let me eat it!

96
00:13:29,709 --> 00:13:31,140
Let's trade lunches!

97
00:13:31,325 --> 00:13:33,560
Looks so good. Let me have some too!

98
00:13:33,680 --> 00:13:36,640
No way! Like I'd ever give any to you guys!

99
00:13:37,095 --> 00:13:38,095
Hand it over!

100
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:38,520
Like hell I will!

101
00:13:38,930 --> 00:13:39,930
Whoops, take that!

102
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:41,820
Why, you little...!

103
00:13:42,685 --> 00:13:43,685
Hah!

104
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:46,280
Ow!

105
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:48,580
Oww!

106
00:13:48,980 --> 00:13:50,200
Oww!

107
00:13:59,985 --> 00:14:01,560
Now then...

108
00:14:04,499 --> 00:14:05,499
Welcome home, Cole.

109
00:14:13,279 --> 00:14:14,900
What happened to your clothes?

110
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:16,980
You've been fighting, haven't you?

111
00:14:17,500 --> 00:14:21,840
Cole loved mischief too, but he was never bad enough to tear his clothes to shreds like this.

112
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:26,880
Oh well.

113
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:29,100
By the way, did you enjoy your lunch?

114
00:14:30,060 --> 00:14:31,060
Yeah.

115
00:14:31,980 --> 00:14:34,600
I'm glad. Now, give me the basket.

116
00:14:36,319 --> 00:14:39,300
What's wrong? Come on, give it here.

117
00:14:42,460 --> 00:14:43,460
Here.

118
00:14:45,369 --> 00:14:50,360
I'm sorry. Everyone tried to take my lunch, so...

119
00:14:50,759 --> 00:14:53,880
You ruin everything that belonged to Cole, don't you?

120
00:14:54,380 --> 00:14:55,380
Huh?

121
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:05,560
Eat up. They're all Cole's favorites.

122
00:15:10,779 --> 00:15:15,020
Mokku, what would you like on your bread? Cole loved jam.

123
00:15:15,625 --> 00:15:18,320
He'd take huge bites, too.

124
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:22,880
Here, I spread plenty of jam on it, just like Cole liked.

125
00:15:26,949 --> 00:15:29,360
What's wrong? You're a strange boy.

126
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:33,520
Mokku!

127
00:15:34,799 --> 00:15:36,140
I don't want that stuff!

128
00:15:37,869 --> 00:15:41,420
Mokku, that is unacceptable! Cole was a much better boy.

129
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,280
Stop it!

130
00:15:45,859 --> 00:15:47,380
Cole! Cole! Cole!

131
00:15:48,269 --> 00:15:49,640
I'm not Cole!

132
00:15:50,060 --> 00:15:51,800
I'm Mokku! My name is Mokku!

133
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:56,100
(Camera shutter clicks)

134
00:16:29,049 --> 00:16:31,640
Ma'am, I'm sorry about earlier.

135
00:16:35,059 --> 00:16:42,760
It's all right, Mokku. Please forgive me for hurting your feelings. I'm truly grateful for your kind heart.

136
00:16:50,489 --> 00:16:54,720
It's getting late. Good night, Mokku.

137
00:17:03,399 --> 00:17:06,599
Mokku, where are you right now?

138
00:17:13,479 --> 00:17:14,880
Grandpa...

139
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:53,780
(Woman laughing)

140
00:18:29,699 --> 00:18:34,180
I'm just a puppet anyway! I'm not a human child!

141
00:18:37,209 --> 00:18:42,740
Everyone's like that. Just because I'm a puppet with no mother, they treat me like I don't matter.

142
00:18:44,229 --> 00:18:46,140
Cole, Crank, all of them...

143
00:18:46,589 --> 00:18:49,960
But I want a mother, too!

144
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:52,040
I want to be a human child!

145
00:19:07,459 --> 00:19:08,980
Stupid! Stupid! Stupid!

146
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:14,600
Huh?

147
00:19:25,659 --> 00:19:33,460
Mokku... You understand what I told you now, don't you? If you stay here any longer, you'll only cause that lady more suffering.

148
00:19:33,999 --> 00:19:41,600
I don't want to hear your preaching, so just shut up! No matter how hard you try, you can't comfort me.

149
00:19:42,124 --> 00:19:44,420
So you're going back to your big brother.

150
00:19:46,529 --> 00:19:51,860
Mokku, please don't leave me. Don't leave me all alone.

151
00:19:54,429 --> 00:19:55,600
Mokku!

152
00:20:00,949 --> 00:20:03,080
Was it just a dream...

153
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:04,420
Big Brother!

154
00:20:16,579 --> 00:20:18,800
Mokku! Mokku came back!

155
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:39,040
He fell!

156
00:20:40,420 --> 00:20:45,500
Grandpa, I'm sorry for not coming home. Are you mad at me, Grandpa?

157
00:20:47,515 --> 00:20:48,515
No, I'm not.

158
00:20:50,580 --> 00:20:51,580
Really?

159
00:20:52,900 --> 00:20:58,820
Truly. But I was very lonely. Still, I'm so glad. You have no idea how happy I am.

160
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:00,440
Grandpa.

161
00:21:04,789 --> 00:21:09,500
Forgive me. Because we're so poor, I can't even pack you a lunch.

162
00:21:09,794 --> 00:21:14,240
I'm a puppet, so I don't need to eat. Just being by your side is enough.

163
00:21:18,880 --> 00:21:19,880
I'm leaving now!

164
00:21:20,889 --> 00:21:22,420
Be careful out there.

165
00:21:32,919 --> 00:21:33,940
Mokku.

166
00:21:42,469 --> 00:21:45,480
Mokku, you must be angry with me for hitting you.

167
00:21:48,069 --> 00:21:52,000
I couldn't take Cole's place after all. I'm sorry.

168
00:21:56,749 --> 00:21:58,460
Here, this is your lunch.

169
00:21:59,820 --> 00:22:04,980
Thank you, Mokku. Thanks to you, I can keep living without grieving forever.

170
00:22:05,459 --> 00:22:07,980
Really? Do you truly mean it?

171
00:22:10,339 --> 00:22:12,640
Promise me you won't be sad anymore.

172
00:22:13,300 --> 00:22:18,660
I promise. In exchange, Mokku, you must study hard and be a good boy.

173
00:22:20,119 --> 00:22:22,540
Yeah. And I'll become human, just like Cole.

174
00:22:24,180 --> 00:22:25,180
Thank you.

175
00:22:28,464 --> 00:22:29,540
Mama.

176
00:22:32,039 --> 00:22:34,720
I've always wanted to call you that just once.

177
00:22:49,899 --> 00:22:52,060
It's a promise, no more crying.

178
00:22:52,459 --> 00:22:54,181
See, even I'm—

179
00:23:01,194 --> 00:23:02,160
(laughter)

180
00:23:02,161 --> 00:23:03,600
See?

181
00:23:03,884 --> 00:23:04,884
(laughter)

182
00:23:07,889 --> 00:23:09,140
Goodbye, Mokku.

183
00:23:12,489 --> 00:23:14,420
(laughter)

184
00:23:22,749 --> 00:23:23,749
Goodbye, Mama.

185
00:23:27,260 --> 00:23:28,260
Mama...

186
00:23:33,539 --> 00:23:39,880
Just as Nora the stray cat said, Mokku is tied to a cross to begin his training to become human.

187
00:23:40,600 --> 00:23:48,500
By the time he realizes it's a wicked scheme by Kenken and his gang, it's too late, and the scorching sun leaves him utterly exhausted.

188
00:23:49,529 --> 00:23:56,040
On top of that, battered by lightning and a great flood, will Mokku have the strength left to survive this ordeal?

189
00:23:56,634 --> 00:23:59,360
Look forward to next week's Kashi no Ki Mokku!

